Stanislav Traykov <stanislavNoeZpam@tortoises.org> writes:
> As it is we have two important elements of the game that would be changed:
> 
> 1. getting one's bag cursed
> 2. looting nested BoH's
> 
> I think #1 is not unbalancing. If one opts for keeping the BoH in a
> sack, the chance that it will get cursed on the two turns it's out is
> minimal. (And two turns is exaggerated time for that operation.)
> 
> It's an option many players don't make because it is boring with the
> current interface, not because it's bad strategy. If convinient means of
> accessing the inner BoH is provided this would be the way to go and BoH
> just won't get cursed--because the game got a better interface, not
> because it was made easier.

Alternatively, you could have it so that if a random curse hits a
container, it goes on (with the same probabilities) to have a chance
to curse the container's contents. Thus, sacking your BoH will only
reduce the chance of its being cursed, not eliminate it.

